course: dictionary
lesson: 8998
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one is meant. «The skater glided across the frozen lake.» With a frozen lake and gliding, a skater is a person moving on skates.
explain: Read the clues before you choose. «The skater did a trick at the skate park.» Skate park is the clue here. Swap in your meaning: a person who rides a skateboard fits, so this is the second meaning.
explain: Some words are part of a longer name. «Pond skaters walk on the water.» Here skater is part of the name of an insect, so the clues are pond and water. When you are unsure, swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A skater is a person who moves on skates: ice skates, roller skates or inline skates.
fact: A skater can also be a person who rides a skateboard, called a skateboarder.
fact: «Figure skaters» and «speed skaters» are two kinds of skater.
fact: «Pond skaters» are insects that rest on the surface of water, and the word skater is part of their name.
fact: Water's surface behaves like a thin, stretchy skin, which is why a pond skater can walk on it.
exercise: «The skater spun fast across the ice rink.» What is a skater here? | A tall tree in the park | A kind of cloud | *A person moving on skates | A type of rowing boat
exercise: «Skaters wear helmets and pads at the skate park.» What do skaters wear to keep safe? | Wellington boots | Swimming goggles | Hats and scarves for the cold | *Helmets and pads
exercise: «Pond skaters walk on the water.» Which of these is a pond skater? | A skateboard trick | *An insect that walks on water | A person on ice skates | A boat with oars
test: «The skateboard skater did a trick at the skate park.» What does skater mean here? | A person who moves on ice skates | *A person who rides a skateboard | A type of park bench | A kind of insect
test: «Skaters balance using the inner ear, eyes and leg muscles.» What helps skaters balance? | Their gloves | Their hats | Their school bags | *The inner ear
exam: «The skater glided across the lake.» Jayden asks how to check the meaning of skater. What is the best way? | Look for the longest word in the sentence | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Read only the title of the text | Ignore the sentence and guess
